        en: "A day for secret beaches. Tucked between Benidorm and Villajoyosa lies Racó de Conill — a crystal-clear cove with no bar or music. Arrive early. Part of the cove is a naturist zone; the atmosphere is calm throughout. Travelling with children? We recommend Aqualandia waterpark in Benidorm (aqualandiabenidorm.com) — tickets bought online are cheaper than at the gate. In the afternoon, Playa Paradís in Villajoyosa: golden sand, shallow water great for children, and far fewer people than Benidorm. Villajoyosa has rows of colourful houses along the seafront and the Valor chocolate factory, with a free museum and tasting. Overnight: Villajoyosa stopover, 5 minutes' walk to the beach.",
